#: include/global_settings.php:2411
msgid "Spike Kill Settings"
msgstr "Ntọala Spike Kill"

#: include/global_settings.php:2416
msgid "Removal Method"
msgstr "Ụzọ Mwepụ"

#: include/global_settings.php:2417
msgid "There are two removal methods.  The first, Standard Deviation, will remove any sample that is X number of standard deviations away from the average of samples.  The second method, Variance, will remove any sample that is X% more than the Variance average.  The Variance method takes into account a certain number of 'outliers'.  Those are exceptional samples, like the spike, that need to be excluded from the Variance Average calculation."
msgstr "Enwere ụzọ mwepụ abụọ. Nke mbụ, Standard Deviation, ga-ewepụ ihe nlele ọ bụla nke dị ọnụọgụ X nke standard deviations pụọ na nkezi nke ihe nlele. Ụzọ nke abụọ, Variance, ga-ewepụ ihe nlele ọ bụla nke dị X% karịa nkezi Variance. Ụzọ Variance na-eburu n'uche ụfọdụ ọnụọgụ nke 'outliers'. Ndị ahụ bụ ihe nlele pụrụ iche, dịka spike, nke kwesịrị ka ewepụ ya na ngụkọ Nkezi Variance."

#: include/global_settings.php:2421
msgid "Standard Deviation"
msgstr "Standard Deviation"

#: include/global_settings.php:2422
msgid "Variance Based w/Outliers Removed"
msgstr "Dabere na Variance nwere Outliers E Wepụrụ"

#: include/global_settings.php:2426 lib/html.php:2668
msgid "Replacement Method"
msgstr "Ụzọ Nnọchi"

#: include/global_settings.php:2427
msgid "There are three replacement methods.  The first method replaces the spike with the average of the data source in question.  The second method replaces the spike with a 'NaN'.  The last replaces the spike with the last known good value found."
msgstr "Enwere ụzọ ndochi atọ. Ụzọ mbụ na-eji nkezi nke isi iyi data a na-ekwu maka ya dochie spike ahụ. Ụzọ nke abụọ na-eji 'NaN' dochie spike ahụ. Nke ikpeazụ na-eji ezigbo ọnụọgụgụ ikpeazụ a maara achọtara dochie spike ahụ."

#: include/global_settings.php:2431 lib/html.php:2664
msgid "Average"
msgstr "Nkezi"

#: include/global_settings.php:2432 lib/html.php:2665
msgid "NaN's"
msgstr "NaN's"

#: include/global_settings.php:2433 lib/html.php:2666
msgid "Last Known Good"
msgstr "Nke Ikpeazụ A Maara Dị Mma"

#: include/global_settings.php:2437
msgid "Number of Standard Deviations"
msgstr "Ọnụọgụgụ Standard Deviations"

#: include/global_settings.php:2438
msgid "Any value that is this many standard deviations above the average will be excluded.  A good number will be dependent on the type of data to be operated on.  We recommend a number no lower than 5 Standard Deviations."
msgstr "Ọnụọgụ ọ bụla karịrị nkezi site na ndịiche ọkọlọtọ ole a ga-ewepụ. Ọnụọgụ dị mma ga-adabere n'ụdị data a ga-arụ ọrụ na ya. Anyị na-akwado ọnụọgụ na-erughị Ndịiche Ọkọlọtọ 5."

#: include/global_settings.php:2442 include/global_settings.php:2443
#: include/global_settings.php:2444 include/global_settings.php:2445
#: include/global_settings.php:2446 include/global_settings.php:2447
#: include/global_settings.php:2448 include/global_settings.php:2449
#: include/global_settings.php:2450 include/global_settings.php:2451
#: include/global_settings.php:2452 include/global_settings.php:2453
#: include/global_settings.php:2454
#, php-format
msgid "%d Standard Deviations"
msgstr "Ndịiche Ọkọlọtọ %d"

#: include/global_settings.php:2458
msgid "Variance Percentage"
msgstr "Pasentị Variance"

#: include/global_settings.php:2459
#, php-format
msgid "This value represents the percentage above the adjusted sample average once outliers have been removed from the sample.  For example, a Variance Percentage of 100%% on an adjusted average of 50 would remove any sample above the quantity of 100 from the graph."
msgstr "Ọnụọgụgụ a na-anọchite anya pasentị karịrị nkezi ihe nlele agbanwere ozugbo ewepụrụ outliers na ihe nlele ahụ. Dịka ọmụmaatụ, Pasentị Variance nke 100%% na nkezi agbanwere nke 50 ga-ewepụ ihe nlele ọ bụla karịrị ọnụọgụ 100 site na eserese ahụ."

#: include/global_settings.php:2482
msgid "Variance Number of Outliers"
msgstr "Ọnụọgụ Variance nke Outliers"

#: include/global_settings.php:2483
msgid "This value represents the number of high and low average samples will be removed from the sample set prior to calculating the Variance Average.  If you choose an outlier value of 5, then both the top and bottom 5 averages are removed."
msgstr "Ọnụọgụgụ a na-anọchite anya ọnụọgụ ihe nlele nkezi dị elu na nke dị ala a ga-ewepụ na setịpụ ihe nlele tupu agbakọọ Nkezi Variance. Ọ bụrụ na ị họrọ ọnụọgụgụ outlier nke 5, mgbe ahụ a ga-ewepụ ma nkezi 5 kachasị elu ma nke kachasị ala."

